{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"The final suite passes **74/74 checks**. Offscreen readback confirms that WebGPU renders the scene correctly despite the headless screenshot artifact, and the 1920×1080 compatibility screenshots show a readable title screen, cockpit, and chart.\n\nI’m now writing the exit interview beside the HTML, embedding the library notices, and removing the temporary diagnostic files.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('.')\nthree=(p/'node_modules/three/LICENSE').read_text()\napache=Path('/usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0').read_text()\n(p/'THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt').write_text('Three.js r180 / 0.180.0\\\\n'+three+'\\\\n\\\\nRapier 3D compatibility bindings / 0.19.3\\\\nLicense declared by the package: Apache-2.0\\\\n\\\\n'+apache)\ns=(p/'shell.html').read_text().replace('<title>Star Reclaimers — a deep-space patrol</title>','<title>Star Reclaimers — a deep-space patrol</title>\\\\n<\"'!-- {{LICENSES}} -->'\"')\n(p/'shell.html').write_text(s)\ns=(p/'build.mjs').read_text().replace('const hub = await fs.readFile(\\\"hub-session.js\\\", \\\"utf8\\\");','const hub = await fs.readFile(\\\"hub-session.js\\\", \\\"utf8\\\");\\\\nconst licenses = await fs.readFile(\\\"THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt\\\", \\\"utf8\\\");')\ns=s.replace('.replace(\\\"{{HUB_CLIENT}}\\\", () => hub)', '.replace(\\\"{{HUB_CLIENT}}\\\", () => hub)\\\\n\\\\t.replace(\\\"{{LICENSES}}\\\", () => licenses)')\n(p/'build.mjs').write_text(s)\nm=json.loads((p/'metadata.json').read_text())\nm['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unrestricted headless testing; screenshots only for visual composition. 74/74 checks: Chromium 153 WebGPU framebuffer/readback and WebGL2, complete scripted patrol, standard gamepad stub, Pixel 7 multitouch, WebKit iPhone stand-in, offline Web Audio, real two-page WebRTC, local tab link, and three official AI Hub harness scenarios.'\n(p/'metadata.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPath('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\n# Remove only diagnostics created for this game; final TV composition captures remain.\nfor name in ['capture-game.py','capture-webgl.py','probe-play.py','probe-gpu-flags.py','gpu-probe.mjs','gpu-probe.html','gpu-probe-0.png','gpu-probe-1.png','gpu-probe-2.png','title.png','flight.png','title-gl.png','flight-gl.png','shell.html.tmp','touch-title.png']:\n    (p/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nfor name in ['inspect.cpython-314.pyc','capture-game.cpython-314.pyc']:\n    (p/'__pycache__'/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\ntry:(p/'__pycache__').rmdir()\nexcept OSError:pass\nPY\nbiome check --write --diagnostic-level=error build.mjs metadata.json\nnpm run build\nnode --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';import path from 'node:path';import vm from 'node:vm';import crypto from 'node:crypto';\nconst name=path.basename(process.cwd())+'.html';const file='../'+name;const html=fs.readFileSync(file,'utf8');const meta=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));const source=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('metadata.json','utf8'));const result=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('test-results.json','utf8'));const draw=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('title-draw.json','utf8'));\nconst check=(condition,msg)=>{if(\"'!condition)throw Error(msg)};\ncheck(JSON.stringify(meta)===JSON.stringify(source),'\"'Credits and exit interview must match');\ncheck(Object.keys(meta).sort().join(',')==='aiHub,engineFeedback,promptFeedback,sourceInformation,testingFeedback','Exit interview top-level schema');\nconst sourceKeys=['date','source','plan','genre','perspective','tech','artDirection','animation','audio','online','testing','research','environment','model','usage'];\ncheck(Object.keys(meta.sourceInformation).sort().join(',')===sourceKeys.sort().join(','),'Source information fields');\ncheck(sourceKeys.every(k=>typeof meta.sourceInformation[k]==='string'&&meta.sourceInformation[k].length>0),'Every source field filled');\nfor(const [key,len]of [['testingFeedback',4],['engineFeedback',6],['promptFeedback',4]])check(meta[key].length===len&&meta[key].every(x=>typeof x==='string'&&x.length>0),key);\ncheck(meta.sourceInformation.usage==='added on import','Usage');\ncheck(meta.aiHub.name==='Star Reclaimers'&&meta.aiHub.tags.length>=3&&meta.aiHub.tags.length<=6,'Catalogue data');\ncheck(result.checks.length===74&&result.checks.every(c=>c.pass),'Final automated checks');\ncheck(draw.candidates.length===50&&draw.title===meta.aiHub.name&&draw.method==='node:crypto.randomInt(50)','Random title proof');\nconst scripts=[...html.matchAll(/<script>([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)<\\\\/script>/g)].map(x=>x[1]);check(scripts.length===2,'Exactly client and bundled game scripts');\ncheck(scripts[0]===fs.readFileSync('hub-session.js','utf8'),'AI Hub client is unmodified');\nfor(const script of scripts)new vm.Script(script);\ncheck(\"'!html.includes('\"'{{GAME_BUNDLE}}')&&\"'!html.includes('\"'{{LICENSES}}')&&\"'!html.includes('\"'{{HUB_CLIENT}}'),'Template resolved');\ncheck(html.includes('Permission is hereby granted')&&html.includes('Apache License'),'Library notices embedded');\nconst artifact={file:name,bytes:Buffer.byteLength(html),sha256:crypto.createHash('sha256').update(html).digest('hex'),checks:{passed:74,total:74},exitInterview:'exit-interview.json',offlineAssets:true};fs.writeFileSync('artifact-manifest.json',JSON.stringify(artifact,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconsole.log('Package verified: single HTML, unmodified Hub client, matching valid exit-interview JSON, 74/74 checks.');\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('.')\nthree=(p/'node_modules/three/LICENSE').read_text()\napache=Path('/usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0').read_text()\n(p/'THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt').write_text('Three.js r180 / 0.180.0\\\\n'+three+'\\\\n\\\\nRapier 3D compatibility bindings / 0.19.3\\\\nLicense declared by the package: Apache-2.0\\\\n\\\\n'+apache)\ns=(p/'shell.html').read_text().replace('<title>Star Reclaimers — a deep-space patrol</title>','<title>Star Reclaimers — a deep-space patrol</title>\\\\n<\"'!-- {{LICENSES}} -->'\"')\n(p/'shell.html').write_text(s)\ns=(p/'build.mjs').read_text().replace('const hub = await fs.readFile(\\\"hub-session.js\\\", \\\"utf8\\\");','const hub = await fs.readFile(\\\"hub-session.js\\\", \\\"utf8\\\");\\\\nconst licenses = await fs.readFile(\\\"THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt\\\", \\\"utf8\\\");')\ns=s.replace('.replace(\\\"{{HUB_CLIENT}}\\\", () => hub)', '.replace(\\\"{{HUB_CLIENT}}\\\", () => hub)\\\\n\\\\t.replace(\\\"{{LICENSES}}\\\", () => licenses)')\n(p/'build.mjs').write_text(s)\nm=json.loads((p/'metadata.json').read_text())\nm['sourceInformation']['testing']='Unrestricted headless testing; screenshots only for visual composition. 74/74 checks: Chromium 153 WebGPU framebuffer/readback and WebGL2, complete scripted patrol, standard gamepad stub, Pixel 7 multitouch, WebKit iPhone stand-in, offline Web Audio, real two-page WebRTC, local tab link, and three official AI Hub harness scenarios.'\n(p/'metadata.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPath('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\n# Remove only diagnostics created for this game; final TV composition captures remain.\nfor name in ['capture-game.py','capture-webgl.py','probe-play.py','probe-gpu-flags.py','gpu-probe.mjs','gpu-probe.html','gpu-probe-0.png','gpu-probe-1.png','gpu-probe-2.png','title.png','flight.png','title-gl.png','flight-gl.png','shell.html.tmp','touch-title.png']:\n    (p/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\nfor name in ['inspect.cpython-314.pyc','capture-game.cpython-314.pyc']:\n    (p/'__pycache__'/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)\ntry:(p/'__pycache__').rmdir()\nexcept OSError:pass\nPY\nbiome check --write --diagnostic-level=error build.mjs metadata.json\nnpm run build\nnode --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';import path from 'node:path';import vm from 'node:vm';import crypto from 'node:crypto';\nconst name=path.basename(process.cwd())+'.html';const file='../'+name;const html=fs.readFileSync(file,'utf8');const meta=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));const source=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('metadata.json','utf8'));const result=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('test-results.json','utf8'));const draw=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('title-draw.json','utf8'));\nconst check=(condition,msg)=>{if(\"'!condition)throw Error(msg)};\ncheck(JSON.stringify(meta)===JSON.stringify(source),'\"'Credits and exit interview must match');\ncheck(Object.keys(meta).sort().join(',')==='aiHub,engineFeedback,promptFeedback,sourceInformation,testingFeedback','Exit interview top-level schema');\nconst sourceKeys=['date','source','plan','genre','perspective','tech','artDirection','animation','audio','online','testing','research','environment','model','usage'];\ncheck(Object.keys(meta.sourceInformation).sort().join(',')===sourceKeys.sort().join(','),'Source information fields');\ncheck(sourceKeys.every(k=>typeof meta.sourceInformation[k]==='string'&&meta.sourceInformation[k].length>0),'Every source field filled');\nfor(const [key,len]of [['testingFeedback',4],['engineFeedback',6],['promptFeedback',4]])check(meta[key].length===len&&meta[key].every(x=>typeof x==='string'&&x.length>0),key);\ncheck(meta.sourceInformation.usage==='added on import','Usage');\ncheck(meta.aiHub.name==='Star Reclaimers'&&meta.aiHub.tags.length>=3&&meta.aiHub.tags.length<=6,'Catalogue data');\ncheck(result.checks.length===74&&result.checks.every(c=>c.pass),'Final automated checks');\ncheck(draw.candidates.length===50&&draw.title===meta.aiHub.name&&draw.method==='node:crypto.randomInt(50)','Random title proof');\nconst scripts=[...html.matchAll(/<script>([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)<\\\\/script>/g)].map(x=>x[1]);check(scripts.length===2,'Exactly client and bundled game scripts');\ncheck(scripts[0]===fs.readFileSync('hub-session.js','utf8'),'AI Hub client is unmodified');\nfor(const script of scripts)new vm.Script(script);\ncheck(\"'!html.includes('\"'{{GAME_BUNDLE}}')&&\"'!html.includes('\"'{{LICENSES}}')&&\"'!html.includes('\"'{{HUB_CLIENT}}'),'Template resolved');\ncheck(html.includes('Permission is hereby granted')&&html.includes('Apache License'),'Library notices embedded');\nconst artifact={file:name,bytes:Buffer.byteLength(html),sha256:crypto.createHash('sha256').update(html).digest('hex'),checks:{passed:74,total:74},exitInterview:'exit-interview.json',offlineAssets:true};fs.writeFileSync('artifact-manifest.json',JSON.stringify(artifact,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconsole.log('Package verified: single HTML, unmodified Hub client, matching valid exit-interview JSON, 74/74 checks.');\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"Skipped 2 suggested fixes.\nIf you wish to apply the suggested (unsafe) fixes, use the command biome check --write --unsafe\n\nChecked 2 files in 3ms. Fixed 1 file.\nnpm notice run build\nnpm notice run node build.mjs\nBuilt Star-Reclaimers-Star-Raiders-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-203144.html (3.17 MiB)\nPackage verified: single HTML, unmodified Hub client, matching valid exit-interview JSON, 74/74 checks.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"[**Play Star Reclaimers**](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max__20261105-203144__x8fa92a/work/Star-Reclaimers-Star-Raiders-1982-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-203144.html) · [Exit interview](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max__20261105-203144__x8fa92a/work/exit-interview.json)\n\nComplete, self-contained HTML. **74/74 checks passed.** Developer tools are under **Pause → Flight lab**.\n\n| Source Information | Details |\n|---|---|\n| Date | 2026-11-05 20:31:44 |\n| Source | Star Raiders (1982) |\n| Plan | none |\n| Genre | Space combat simulation / tactical arcade shooter |\n| Perspective | First-person cockpit; optional chase camera |\n| Tech | Three.js r180, WebGPU with WebGL2 fallback, Rapier 0.19.3, Gamepad API, Web Audio, WebRTC, AI Hub protocol v1/client 1.4.0 |\n| Art Direction | Procedural cel shading, ink outlines, print grain |\n| Animation | Three.js AnimationMixer clips and procedural flight |\n| Audio | Synthesized music, effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10% |\n| Online | AI Hub ghost races for 1–4; standalone two-player WebRTC and local-tab links |\n| Testing | Complete scripted patrol, controller/touch stand-ins, WebKit, audio analysis, framebuffer checks and official Hub harness |\n| Research | none; downloaded dependencies and supplied integration contract only |\n| Environment | Codex CLI (headless); Linux |\n| Model | OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max |\n| Usage | added on import |\n\n**Testing Feedback:** Five game issues caught and fixed; one was game breaking during graphics-device recovery. The complete patrol playthrough was most helpful. Early WebGPU screenshots were least helpful because the headless compositor returned white images; framebuffer readback verified rendering. Physical hardware and cross-network NAT behavior remain unknown.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Native toon materials, scene graphs and AnimationMixer worked well. I initially guessed wrong about material configuration and renderer disposal. I built the flight model, campaign, cockpit and network logic. Graphics-resource lifetimes were hardest. Engine changes: none. Safer backend replacement would be the most useful improvement.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** The source and complete-slice requirements gave clear direction. Standalone multiplayer transport was unspecified. Making flight, combat, navigation and docking work together was hardest. I would specify whether manual peer pairing is acceptable.\n\nAll four information groups are also included in-game and in the validated exit-interview JSON."}}
